commit 4f180240fec05d268b73d835120787a0d0080e60

C03: software.python.status reads the Python installs registered in Windows (SYSTEM1697)

«dime la versión de Python instalada» (H0307) reached no operation. The new read-only operation software.python.status (Kernel descriptor, Core handler list, WindowsDeviceControlAdapter.PythonStatus) enumerates the PEP 514 registrations under Software\Python of the current user and the machine (WOW6432Node included): company, tag, version, display name and whether the registered executable exists — read from the registry only, no interpreter started. The mind reads the version question (Spanish and English; never install, update, run or pip) as that operation with no arguments, the composer answers with the exact registered version strings, newest first, or says none is registered, and the vetoes reject a version number the registry did not carry or a reply without the version.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


